From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SenkOS
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] input: adc-joystick: invert by the axis' code, not the
 channel's index

adc_joystick_invert() looks up the axis' range by its ABS code, but both
callers pass the channel's index. That only works while channel n reports
code n: with four channels for ABS_X, ABS_Y, ABS_RX, ABS_RY, an inverted
third channel reads ABS_Z's range (0, 0) and reports -val.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/adc-joystick.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/adc-joystick.c
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return;
 		if (joy->axes[i].inverted)
-			val = adc_joystick_invert(input, i, val);
+			val = adc_joystick_invert(input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 		input_report_abs(input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 	}
 	input_sync(input);
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@
 		else
 			val &= GENMASK(msb, 0);
 		if (joy->axes[i].inverted)
-			val = adc_joystick_invert(joy->input, i, val);
+			val = adc_joystick_invert(joy->input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 		input_report_abs(joy->input, joy->axes[i].code, val);
 	}
 
